  "observations": [
    "Target getter returns raw viewport target and reports/repairs mirror only on coordinate inequality; NaN always unequal, signed zeros compare equal. Setter always copies resulting viewport target to mirror even when request rejects.",
    "SetScreenPort rejects equal horizontal or vertical bounds before mutation. Otherwise accepts reversed bounds, writes both depths only if either request is nonzero and sets valid=true. The merge zero-port call therefore leaves all saved port fields unchanged.",
    "TrimLeftAndRight invokes right trimming then tail-calls left trimming; default trim set is exactly space/tab/CR/LF. IsEmpty tests stored length; wide Compare uses unsigned UTF16 units and stops at NUL (or handles a NUL-leading comparison target through length). The optimized clean-name predicate preserves these edges.",
    "SetView is a1068-byte concrete operation, not whole-view assignment. It validates input/page-main basis, copies viewport, preserves/restores existing viewport UUID, selects parent-dependent view kind/page/position/cplane, invokes name/image/display operations and notifies document.",
    "SetScreenSize is543 bytes: guard dimensions>1 and changed cached size, set screen port/aspect, actual wallpaper resize, serial/cache matrix/screen updates. These concrete collaborators remain required before actual Pop."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Resolve SetView validation0x26a400 and UUID preservation0x26a280, image/display/name operations and actual parent/document lifetimes.",
    "Implement concrete screen-aspect/wallpaper/cache effects and window client-size provider; no success callbacks standing in for them.",
    "Actual Pop must remove/update cursor and returnfalse after mutation as original."
  ],
  "scope": "Static original source evidence and merge prerequisite only, not original runtime/full restoration/PC/physical equivalence."
}
